            <div xml:id="d220">

                <pb facs="0277" n="177" xml:id="pg177"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/24359: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-17T13:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17, 1920—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>331. <hi rendition="#italic">El Democrata</hi> today publishes the statement that
                    the Government of Venezuela has decided that Constitutional order has not been
                    interrupted in Mexico and consequently has recognized the Mexican Government of
                    Substitute President de la Huerta. The Foreign Office has advised me informally
                    that this statement is correct.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
